AWS Shared Responsibility Model: What AWS Manages vs. What You Manage

One of the most fundamental concepts in AWS security and compliance is the Shared Responsibility Model.
It clearly defines the line between what AWS secures for you, and what you must secure yourself.

🔹 AWS Responsibility (“Security of the Cloud”)

Physical infrastructure (data centers, networking, hardware)

Global infrastructure (Regions, Availability Zones, Edge Locations)

Managed services infrastructure (compute, storage, networking)


🔹 Customer Responsibility (“Security in the Cloud”)

Identity & Access Management (IAM users, roles, policies)

Application security (patching OS, securing code, configs)

Data protection (encryption, backups, key management)

Network configuration (security groups, firewalls, VPC settings)


👉 Why this matters for you?

Interviewers often test this concept to check if you understand where your accountability lies.

In real-world usage, misunderstanding this boundary can lead to security gaps.


